  {
   "topic": "Technology",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "A low-voltage trench MOSFET whose cells are packed densely to bring RDS(ON) down; it is offered for fast switching. Listed applications are battery protection, load switches and power management."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Gate drive",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "The threshold falls between 0.4 V and 1 V (0.6 V typical) at 250 µA, and on-resistance is specified down to 1.8 V of gate drive: 46 mΩ max at 2.7 A. At 4.5 V and 4.5 A it is 25 mΩ max, 20 mΩ typical. The gate is rated ±10 V, leaks at most ±100 nA at that voltage, and has 2.7 Ω of internal resistance typical. In Fig.5 RDS(ON) climbs steeply once VGS drops below about 2 V and is near 20 mΩ from 6 V up."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Temperature",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "On-resistance rises with junction temperature; at 4.5 V gate drive Fig.6 runs from about 0.74 of its normalised value at -55 °C to about 1.66 at 148 °C. Fig.2 shows the 150 °C transfer curve conducting at a lower gate voltage than the 25 °C curve, the two crossing near 1.85 V and 17 A."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Heat",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Junction-to-ambient thermal resistance is 125 °C/W. Power dissipation is 1 W at 25 °C ambient and 0.4 W at 100 °C; continuous drain current falls from 4.5 A to 2.8 A over the same range. Junction and storage temperature both span -55 °C to +150 °C."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Body diode",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "The source-to-drain diode carries 4.5 A continuously and drops 0.9 V typical, 1.2 V max, at 4.5 A. Recovering from 4.5 A at 150 A/µs it takes 17.9 ns and 1.38 nC typical."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Switching",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "With 4.5 V on the gate, 10 V on the drain, 4.5 A and a 3 Ω gate source resistance, delay and transition times are 4.2 ns on-delay, 19.8 ns rise, 22.6 ns off-delay and 23.2 ns fall, all typical. Gate charge to 4.5 V is 6.06 nC, of which 1.07 nC is gate-source and 1.95 nC gate-drain; the Miller plateau in Fig.4 sits near 1.66 V."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Construction",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "SOT-23 case in a UL 94V-0 rated molding compound, RoHS compliant and free of halogens. The leads are solder plated and meet the MIL-STD-750 Method 2026 solderability test. The top face carries the marking 2300."
  }
